<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI PORT HANDLES 83,968 TONNES CARGO.</title>
<headline>KARACHI PORT HANDLES 83,968 TONNES CARGO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 83,968 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 56,227 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     August 11</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 3,060	 2,991</p>
<p>    Import cargo		80,908	53,236</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, two are expected to sail and two are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	18,600	 Kristal		   14/8</p>
<p>Tallow		  6,000	 Jian She		  14/8</p>
<p>Jet fuel	     25,000	 Keefan		    14/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom (9221) 5685192; Fax (9221) 5673428</p>
</text>
